Package: STATassist
Title: Standardised Statistical Comparison Workflows
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: 
    person("Wonseok", "Oh", , "hiows97@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0002-0687-8466"))
Description: Runs every test applicable to a comparison through a single
    function call and returns standardised, feature-wise result tables. Two-group
    comparison reports parametric, rank-based and robust results side by side,
    together with fold changes, effect estimates, confidence intervals and
    multiplicity adjusted p-values, so that a conclusion is never based on a
    single test. Significance tables and volcano, boxplot and back-to-back
    histogram visualisations are derived from the same result object, which keeps
    effect sizes and p-values describing the same observations. The implemented
    methods include those described by Welch (1947)
    <doi:10.1093/biomet/34.1-2.28>, Wilcoxon (1945) <doi:10.2307/3001968>, Mann
    and Whitney (1947) <doi:10.1214/aoms/1177730491>, Yuen (1974)
    <doi:10.1093/biomet/61.1.165>, Brunner and Munzel (2000)
    <doi:10.1002/(SICI)1521-4036(200001)42:1%3C17::AID-BIMJ17%3E3.0.CO;2-U>, and
    Algina, Keselman and Penfield (2005) <doi:10.1037/1082-989X.10.3.317>.
